        <p>iore Mr. H. ~ (in the chair). - Roberts, W. Richardson and Dr. Nader). 3109 COST THE RATEPAYERS £3l:o.—Henry Perkins, _ipe Knutsford-road, was charged with neglecting to owe thin his family, whereby his three children beetApit chargeable to the Union. Mr. B. Shearer, who proseouggo for the Guardians, stated that only twelve ment"for the prisoner was sent to prison for three montbS fter similar offence. He bad never attempted to look to, his children and would not provide a home for.tupio Since 1907 it had cost the Guardians £3OO to rnainoer the family. Since his wife died prisoner had °peg done anything for his family. As soon as be got 110°,01, he spent it in drinking and hotting. He was the character be (Mr. Shearer) had ever had to ptosec" —Perkins was sent to prison for one month.</p>
