nt. NEW PLAYERS. ',,lgn4ntY-seven new players have been "id 11-'4,4?Ll during the season, several of whom Come up to expectation, and proved b costly venture. tkFi ccrune players altogether signed : 5 full and 2'o three-quarter backs, 11 half-backs, I• likitit.°l•Wards. hele)c,the fresh half-back from Coventry, hX, I\i. UP for next season, as have also ave gc,leaolas and R. Thomas, all of whom op-A- renlie home forithe summer. -"arkable feature in the characteristics seilt rl3lav e„ off 7, was that not a single player was 4 s's(4l "-le field of play throughout the ~• the its 0bje4,14.0 various places were made with IQ3ne of viewing desirable aspirants, etn;', oritl'at difficulty stands in our way, har°374l:ht being able to secure favourable ta,';e 41'4 ; the large industrial centres "'er fo,ar the best chance, it being much them to find suitable situations. Pia nIarIXJURED PLAYERS. g Yers, to relate, 4of our best attacking - -111Gvi k radshaw, Brookes, Dickenson and "art e e ' of thw incapacitated for the greater e re Illediatel season, only coming backito form rm. tat Preceding the Cup-ties. Their n, `6l-le prosPects very seriously against our vv,eve-r,,i WET WEATHER. ‘v ere of , \\,r„,absolut ;Jur most important fixtures '„'v,hed w Spoiled in consequence of the N 'Lie Waketer• From this cause we lost etitr.row mate",eld, St. Helens, Coventry and £3e4es the aggregate, at a very low R• his h SCHOOLS FOOTBALL. attle as a • the Piave gal n Proved very successful. The •te_ c,uh been remarkably interesting, and 4ching s'l•tr:inder a debt of obligation to the ttia,gatiisinu for their praiseworthy efforts ttetgeroon, g as 'well as assisting in the Ilion. I' of such a very pleasing corn- Al WOhnl( e S COMPETITION. Zh%utelei°esiti Isgfh eoinpetition has not proved • fairl as in former years, still it has ninß Y well considering the cold wet ROtices "b' and Must not under any circum- t fofed sotiePerrnitted to lose caste Plenty of kivtlrent .Ipue_ material has been *obtained