        <head>WOMEN LIBERALS.</head>
        <p>WOMEN LIBERALS.</p>
        <p>Delegates Representing 130.000 Members Meet in London. --- WARRINGTON THE LARGEST ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>BY MRS. OSBORNE. Annual Council Meetings of the Women s ;1-1, ineFeendte Square,ratio nwere held. in the "orticultural London, on May oth, 7th and rep :,,he.ll upwards of 900 delegates were present, tf,:nling 815 iissociations with a total membership layv:. During the year 34 new ciations qara j°ined the Federation. Great activity has part c.terisEd the doings of the Federation, and sa of the crusade scheme 76,000 leaflets on subjects ~• eul politics have been circulated monthly in gil,,,enostitileticies, and official assistance has been Wa-11. to Liberal candidates in 12 by-elections. ri. D.-,,,,Tgton Women's Liberal A.ssoriation has the membership any of the affiliated a,s',ciA- Was represented at the confetence by Miss Ifrrs-'ad, Mrs. O'Brien, Mrs. T. Lccker, Mrs. Lindley, • Dutton, and myself. WOMAN SUFFRAGE. Conntess of Carlisle'took the chair rech day at lipi-j4a and the big hall was crowded, many women si,e linable to find seats. The discussion on Woman triit age took up the whole of the first day. It is the the :iceaaion that so much time has been devoted to \l'hi4h-e,stinn, and it shows pretty clearly the interest opirk 's being taken in the cause. No difference of the tha merits of Woman's Suffrage w•qi shcwn ; the 'Peeches were pro and con amendments to W.L'- Arules affecting it. The Tunbridge Wells arldt3, atter cOnsultatiou with Airs. Eva McLaren tent e other signatories, and with the coo- the. Grimsby Association had decided oa amendment in the following form : tbern°l, W°nlen's Liberal Association is eligible for ahstsershiP of the Federation which is not prepared to is c'n frern working for any Liberal candidate who Asse°„t,able to sati4v the Executive Committee of the 144-Cation that he'is determined, if returned to Parlia- ever,' t° Promote the enfranchisement of women by Mean.. ith • e . `, n his power. anldrs.,ll;tre;te.st taken in the discussion was enormous, retie Linue spirited debates it created will be long pop. 'l\ NIcIeeREN, tha