      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0184" n="art0184">
        <p>Sale by Auction.</p>
        <p>By 118. ROBERT LOWE.</p>
        <p>BY ORDER OF THE EXECUTORS.</p>
        <p>TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION by Mr. ROBERT LOWE at the BLUE BELL INN, Horseinarket- street, Warrington, on WEDNESDAY, the 21st day of MAY, 1913, at 3 o'clock in the afternoon precisely. All that detached modern RESIDENCE known as "THE DEL PH," Hill Cliffs., Appleton, Cheshire, recently erected and late in the occupation of the owner, E. CALDWELL, Esq. The house contains large entrance hall, 2 entertaining rooms, kitchen, 'scullery, cellar, wash-house and (self contaked) usual out houses, 5 bedrooms, bath and w.e., and stands in the centre of a well-kept garden. Contents 4940 square yards. Term, leasehold for 999 sears from 1907, ground rent ..£l9. N.B.—This rent covers another building plot adjoin- ing the plot on which the house stands, which can be sub-leased if desired. _ _ _ . _</p>
        <p>The property is beautifully situated on the Cheshire border, about two miles from Warrington. It stands very high, is well and substantially built on a zed sand- stone foundation, commands an extensive view of an undulating and well-wooded country, and is within two minutes' walk from the Warrington Golf Links ats Appleton, an excellent IS-hoie course. Photograph sent on application. For further particulars and order to view, apply to the Auctioneer, No. 1, Bank-street, Warrington ; or to— CHAS. H. UNSWORTH, Golden Square, Solicitor for the Vendors. Market Place, Warrington.</p>
      </div>
